On staging, the deployment now reaches the private ops container successfully, but the packaged Drizzle process exits with status 1 and its useful error is currently discarded. I’m applying the repository’s Effect guidance to add safe failure classification, so the next deployment tells us whether this is TLS, authentication, network access, or a missing runtime artifact without leaking credentials.","phase":"commentary"},{"type":"agentMessage","id":"item-4595","text":"The recovery run confirmed this is not an HTTP/auth/route failure: `/healthz` is healthy and authenticated ops requests arrive, but Drizzle itself exits. I’ve moved onto a fresh branch at the exact merged `main`; an untracked Terraform working directory appeared from the earlier read-only inspection, so I’m separating generated cache from source before touching application code.","phase":"commentary"},{"type":"reasoning","id":"item-4596","summary":["**Tracing .gitignore differences in PR squash merge**","**Investigating git index skip-worktree flags**","**Diagnosing stale local main branching issue**","**Planning command failure classification implementation**","**Designing error classification and logging enhancements**","**Categorizing error patterns from PostgreSQL messages**","**Designing error classification and logging enhancements**","**Categorizing error patterns from PostgreSQL messages**","**Designing error classification and logging enhancements**","**Categorizing error patterns from PostgreSQL messages**","**Implementing structured error classification and Effect-based failure handling**"]},{"type":"agentMessage","id":"item-4597","text":"The code path now narrows the likely failure to four concrete classes. The strongest architectural suspicion is verified TLS against a private-IP endpoint, because Terraform deliberately builds the URL from the database’s private-network IP. I’m checking Scaleway’s current certificate/private-network contract before deciding whether to fix the endpoint itself or first ship diagnostics.","phase":"commentary"},{"type":"webSearch","id":"exec-66843c8d-92a6-46e4-b355-04f4e74b46e9","query":"site:scaleway.com/en/docs managed database PostgreSQL private network TLS certificate IP certificate verify hostname ...","action":{"type":"search","query":null,"queries":["site:scaleway.com/en/docs managed database PostgreSQL private network TLS certificate IP certificate verify hostname","site:registry.terraform.io/providers/scaleway/scaleway scaleway_rdb_instance certificate private_network ip","site:github.com/scaleway/terraform-provider-scaleway rdb_instance certificate private_network ip TLS"]}},{"type":"reasoning","id":"item-4598","summary":["**Deciding to use provider hostname for private network**"]},{"type":"webSearch","id":"exec-faa4afec-c357-4b84-b97a-1ef193f9c91b","query":"site:scaleway.com/en/docs/managed-databases-for-postgresql-and-mysql TLS certificate sslmode verify-full hostname private network PostgreSQL ...","action":{"type":"search","query":null,"queries":["site:scaleway.com/en/docs/managed-databases-for-postgresql-and-mysql TLS certificate sslmode verify-full hostname private network PostgreSQL","site:scaleway.com/en/docs/managed-databases-for-postgresql-and-mysql "sslmode" "verify"","site:github.com/scaleway "private_network[0].hostname" database terraform"]}},{"type":"webSearch","id":"exec-13fb38ac-7a0c-4cdc-8903-1ad0d669b40f","query":""rw-${instance_id}.rdb.${region}.scw.cloud" private network Scaleway ...","action":{"type":"search","query":null,"queries":[""rw-${instance_id}.rdb.${region}.scw.cloud" private network Scaleway","site:github.com/scaleway "rw-" ".rdb." "private_network"","site:github.com/scaleway/terraform-provider-scaleway rdb hostname rw-"]}},{"type":"reasoning","id":"item-4599","summary":["**Planning SSL servername injection**","**Planning TLS serverName fix and diagnostics**","**Planning TLS servername configuration**","**Constructing canonical server name**","**Adding DATABASE_TLS_SERVER_NAME with validation**","**Planning tests and Terraform servername interpolation**","**Adding DATABASE_TLS_SERVER_NAME with validation**","**Planning tests and Terraform servername interpolation**","**Adding DATABASE_TLS_SERVER_NAME with validation**","**Planning tests and Terraform servername interpolation**","**Designing TLS config tests and failure classification**","**Adding DATABASE_TLS_SERVER_NAME with validation**","**Planning tests and Terraform servername interpolation**","**Designing TLS config tests and failure classification**"]},{"type":"agentMessage","id":"item-4600","text":"The likely root cause is now concrete: Scaleway’s verified-full certificate expects `rw-<database-id>.rdb.fr-par.scw.cloud`, while our app connects to the private IP and gives Node no TLS server name. That makes certificate identity verification fail even though the private route and CA are correct. I’m fixing this by keeping the private IP for routing and supplying the canonical Scaleway hostname as SNI/certificate identity; I’m also adding redacted failure categories so any remaining ops error is actionable.","phase":"commentary"},{"type":"fileChange","id":"exec-28d263d4-ffde-4a01-9e8c-cdbef1f691e8","status":"completed","changes":[{"path":"/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/b7e9/evorto/helpers/database.ts","kind":{"type":"update","move_path":null}},{"path":"/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/b7e9/evorto/migration/index.ts","kind":{"type":"update","move_path":null}},{"path":"/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/b7e9/evorto/src/db/database-client.ts","kind":{"type":"update","move_path":null}},{"path":"/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/b7e9/evorto/src/db/database-config.spec.ts","kind":{"type":"update","move_path":null}},{"path":"/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/b7e9/evorto/src/db/database-config.ts","kind":{"type":"update","move_path":null}},{"path":"/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/b7e9/evorto/src/db/database.layer.ts","kind":{"type":"update","move_path":null}},{"path":"/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/b7e9/evorto/