On Portless: I like it as a local-development pilot. It gives each worktree a stable HTTPS hostname, allowing Auth0 configuration such as an exact base callback plus `https://*.evorto.localhost/callback`. Auth0 supports a single leftmost-label wildcard, which fits this model. I would keep CI on fixed localhost ports initially because Portless is still pre-1.0. [Portless](https://github.com/vercel-labs/portless), [Auth0 wildcard guidance](https://auth0.com/docs/get-started/applications/wildcards-for-subdomains)

